<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">04032026</say-as>.</s> <s>The fifteenth of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s> <s>It's morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>The United States struck two thousand targets inside Iran on day four of Operation Epic Fury, as B-52 strategic bombers joined a campaign that Iran's Red Crescent says has killed seven hundred and eighty-seven people.</s> <s>United States Central Command's commander described the assault as double the scale of the two thousand and three Iraq invasion — a comparison that signals intent, not restraint.</s> <s>Iran struck back with missiles that hit <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="æl juːˈdeɪd">Al-Udeid</phoneme> Air Base in Qatar, and neither side has offered ceasefire terms.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israeli airstrikes killed fifty people in Lebanon, including seven children, as a ground offensive displaced fifty-eight thousand in two days.</s> <s>Hezbollah official <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="moʊhɑːˈmuːd koʊˈmɑː.ti">Mohamoud Komati</phoneme> declared open war after Israel struck <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈbɑːl.bɛk">Baalbek</phoneme> and continued to hold five border positions it was due to vacate after November's ceasefire, signaling it intends to dismantle Hezbollah permanently rather than return to the pre-war line.</s> <s>Syria has moved rockets to its Lebanese border — telling Beirut the weapons guard against Hezbollah, not Israel — leaving the country's south contested by three armed forces with no ceasefire among any of them.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Sudan, the Rapid Support Forces blacked out the city of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɛl oʊˈbeɪd">El-Obeid</phoneme> using drone strikes, targeting the supply crossroads that connects their Darfur stronghold to army-held territory.</s> <s>This is a central front in a war that has displaced eleven million people — one of the world's largest displacement crises, rarely treated as such.</s> <s>The paramilitaries have struck El-Obeid three times since January, and no peace talks are scheduled.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Democratic senators emerged from a classified military briefing fearing President Trump is planning a ground invasion of Iran.</s> <s>Senator Tim Kaine invoked the nineteen seventy-three War Powers Resolution, which would require the president to cease operations within sixty days without congressional authorization — a veto override requires two-thirds of both chambers.</s> <s>Two thousand targets have already been struck; the resolution has not yet passed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Spain remains the last North Atlantic Treaty Organization ally to refuse opening its military bases to American bombers targeting Iran, and President Trump threatened to cut all trade with Madrid in retaliation.</s> <s>The United Kingdom reversed its position under pressure, leaving Spain isolated; Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent was tasked with drawing up the sanctions.</s> <s>Refusing to join a war now carries its own economic price.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nepal votes tomorrow in its first election since protests that killed seventy-seven people toppled the government last September.</s> <s>New parties born from those streets — including one led by thirty-five-year-old <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="bɑˈlɛn.drɑ ʃɑː">Balendra Shah</phoneme> — challenge a political class that has cycled through thirty-two governments since nineteen ninety.</s> <s>Nearly one million newly registered young voters will decide whether that cycle breaks, while artificial intelligence deepfakes are already targeting them online.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Strait of Hormuz has seen zero ships for four days — a waterway that carries twenty percent of the world's oil and gas.</s> <s>Oil has reached eighty-five dollars a barrel and European natural gas surged forty percent in two days; central banks cannot cut rates to cushion the blow because energy-driven inflation makes cheaper credit inflationary, not stimulative.</s> <s>Sixteen hundred Malaysian pilgrims remain stranded in Saudi Arabia, unable to return home, with no reopening date announced.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea's stock exchange triggered a circuit breaker Tuesday morning after shares fell eight percent, halting trading for twenty minutes.</s> <s>The country imports virtually all its oil, and the four-day Hormuz closure has cut off its primary energy supply; the won briefly broke one thousand five hundred per dollar — a seventeen-year low.</s> <s>The Bank of Korea warned of excessive currency volatility, and the conflict has no end date in sight.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Indonesia approved construction of its first nuclear power plant on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈbæŋ.kɑ bəˈliː.tʊŋ">Bangka Belitung</phoneme> island, chosen for its rare seismic stability in an archipelago that straddles the Ring of Fire.</s> <s>ThorCon will build the five-hundred-megawatt plant by twenty thirty-two as Indonesia pursues forty-four gigawatts of nuclear capacity to meet electricity demand growing at five percent a year.</s> <s>Southeast Asia's most populous nation has committed to atomic energy on one of the earth's most seismically active zones.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Scientists have solved a long-standing puzzle about the Sun: during its quiet phases, anomalous vibrations disrupted its normal oscillation pattern in ways no model had predicted.</s> <s>A helium layer deep inside ran hotter than expected, causing trapped sound waves to travel faster and shift the oscillation signature — a method called helioseismology that maps the Sun's interior from the outside.</s> <s>The PLATO space mission, launching in twenty twenty-seven, will apply the same technique to read the interiors of other stars.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A study published in Nature shows that proteins inside living cells exploit quantum tunneling to accelerate enzyme reactions, overturning the assumption that biological noise destroys quantum effects before they can do useful work.</s> <s>Protein scaffolds reduce tunneling barriers rather than collapsing quantum states — something previously thought impossible in the warm, chaotic interior of a cell.</s> <s>The finding points toward drug design that works with quantum chemistry, potentially unlocking reaction pathways conventional pharmacology cannot reach.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Every time a phone displays an advertisement, it runs an instant auction that broadcasts the device's precise location to dozens of potential buyers — and an internal Department of Homeland Security document confirms that United States Customs and Border Protection sourced that data to track people's movements, without warrants.</s> <s>The department's inspector general found three agencies used the system illegally.</s> <s>American border surveillance has been running on the mechanics of the advertising economy, no court orders required.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The European Union stripped seven strategic technologies from its industrial plan after Germany and pro-market member states blocked measures to compete with China's state-backed chip and artificial intelligence industries.</s> <s>Now covering only steel and solar panels, the plan leaves Europe dependent on China for the very technologies that will define the next economic era.</s> <s>Brussels chose market orthodoxy at the moment Beijing chose to win.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A hacking toolkit built for the United States government to exploit iPhones has leaked to Russian intelligence, and from there to criminal hackers who used it to infect forty-two thousand devices.</s> <s>Google traced the toolkit, called <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɔˈruː.nɑ">Coruna</phoneme>, from a United States surveillance vendor through a Russian spy group to profit-driven hackers — a cascade that shows government-built cyberweapons rarely stay contained.</s> <s>Apple patched the vulnerabilities in iOS 26; anyone still running iOS 17.2.1 or earlier remains exposed.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We return this evening, as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme> approaches <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑːɡɹɪb">Maghrib</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>